glowing warm globe table lamp and potted greenery. On the right side, light wooden wall-mounted shelves hold upright books, dark ceramic objects and a trailing green plant. Further right, a computer monitor on a wooden desk displays photo-editing software showing a mountain-lake landscape photograph, with a slim backlit monitor light bar mounted above it and a dark keyboard below. The lighting is warm and soft, amber from the left and neutral white from the monitor on the right, with the host lit evenly and brightly from the front. It stays unchanged throughout the clip and no additional environment is introduced.\n\nlighting_and_exposure:\nThe lighting and exposure of the final clip must match <Picture 1> exactly. Keep the image bright, clean and evenly lit, with open shadows and faithful, natural skin tones on <Subject 1>'s face. The host's face must stay clearly visible and well lit from the first frame to the last frame. Do not darken the image. Do not use low-key, moody or underexposed lighting. Do not crush the shadows, do not add deep shadow in the corners, and do not reduce overall brightness or contrast compared with <Picture 1>. Do not introduce neon signage or coloured accent lighting.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reuse] A 9:16 vertical digital-human talking-head clip in a single uninterrupted shot. <Subject 1> (S1) is seated in the setting of <Subject 2>, which is kept exactly as in <Picture 1>, and speaks straight to the camera in Mandarin Chinese while presenting with small, controlled hand gestures. The visual composition remains identical to <Picture 1> from the first frame to the last frame, and the brightness and colour must stay equal to <Picture 1> throughout. The distance between the camera and S1 remains constant for the entire clip. As the only visible speaker, his mouth, jaw, breath pauses and expression follow the actual vocal activity in <Audio 1>, which is reused 1:1 as the complete final audio track. Clean, frameless footage